{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ידעת איש", :translit "yeda'at ish", :gloss "you have known a man"} {:he "אין בתוליה חוזרין", :translit "ein betuleha chozerin", :gloss "her virginity does not return"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ידעת איש", :b "אין בתוליה חוזרין"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'her virginity does not return' reflects the halakhic principle that once a woman's virginity is lost it cannot be restored (Ketubot 11a, Yevamot 59b). The gematria equating 'has known a man' with 'her virginity does not return' underscores the irreversibility implied by the verse's language.", :sources ["Ketubot 11a" "Yevamot 59b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "יודעת", :translit "yoda'at", :gloss "knowing"} {:he "דיבש גלעד", :translit "divsh gil'ad", :gloss "Devash Gil'ad"} {:he "נפלאים מעשיך ונפשי יודעת מאד", :translit "nifla'im ma'asekha venafshi yoda'at me'od", :gloss "Your deeds are wondrous and my soul knows exceedingly"} {:he "שהעבירום לפני הציץ", :translit "shehe'eviram lifnei hatzitz", :gloss "that they passed them before the Tzitz"} {:he "כל שפניה מוריקות", :translit "kol shefanehah morikot", :gloss "all whose face turns green"} {:he "בידוע שנבעלה", :translit "beyado'ah sheniv'alah", :gloss "it is known that she was violated"} {:he "נפלאים מעשיך", :translit "nifla'im ma'asekha", :gloss "Your deeds are wondrous"} {:he "יודעת איש", :translit "yoda'at ish", :gloss "has known a man"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["יודעת" "דיבש גלעד" "נפלאים מעשיך ונפשי יודעת מאד"]}], :frame {:text "The Talmud (Yevamot 60b) discusses how the Israelites identified which captive Midianite women were permissible: they were passed before the Tzitz (the High Priest's headplate), and a woman whose face turned green was thereby revealed to have been violated. Ba'al HaTurim connects the Masorah list's third occurrence — 'Your deeds are wondrous and my soul knows exceedingly' (Psalms 139:14) — to this procedure, reading it as an allusion to how through wondrous divine means it becomes known whether a woman 'has known a man.' The phrase 'Devash Gil'ad' refers to the distinctive plene spelling of the word in that occurrence.", :sources ["Yevamot 60b" "Psalms 139:14"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וכל אשה יודעת איש למשכב", :translit "vechol isha yoda'at ish lemishkav", :gloss "and every woman who has known a man for lying"} {:he "אם היא בת שלש שנים ויום אחד", :translit "im hi bat shalosh shanim veyom echad", :gloss "if she is a girl of three years and one day"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "וכל אשה יודעת איש למשכב", :b "אם היא בת שלש שנים ויום אחד"}], :frame {:text "The age of three years and one day is the halakhic threshold specified in the Mishnah (Niddah 5:4) below which a girl's virginity is legally considered restorable, so that intercourse does not permanently disqualify her. The gematria equating the verse's phrase with this formula signals that the Torah's language inherently encodes this age distinction.", :sources ["Niddah 5:4" "Ketubot 11a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ולא נפקד ממנו איש", :translit "velo nifkad mimenu ish", :gloss "and not a man was missing from us"} {:he "לעבירות", :translit "le'averot", :gloss "for transgressions"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ולא נפקד ממנו איש", :b "לעבירות"}], :frame nil}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "ידעת איש", :a-value 795, :b "אין בתוליה חוזרין", :b-value 795, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["יודעת" "דיבש גלעד" "נפלאים מעשיך ונפשי יודעת מאד"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "יודעת", :refs ["Genesis 4:9" "Genesis 12:11" "Genesis 18:19" "Genesis 20:6" "Genesis 21:26" "Genesis 22:12" "Genesis 27:2" "Genesis 28:16"], :n 254, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "דיבש גלעד", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "נפלאים מעשיך ונפשי יודעת מאד", :refs ["Psalms 139:14"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :gematria, :a "וכל אשה יודעת איש למשכב", :a-value 1555, :b "אם היא בת שלש שנים ויום אחד", :b-value 1564, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "ולא נפקד ממנו איש", :a-value 718, :b "לעבירות", :b-value 718, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:32:24.437143338Z", :model "glm-5.2"}